# Line endings are pinned to LF, matching the 0.3.x repository's policy so the
# two source trees diff cleanly line for line.
#
# The machine this was written on has core.autocrlf=true, so without this file
# a checkout rewrites the working tree to CRLF. Nothing in this build breaks on
# CRLF -- there are no shell scripts here, which is what CRLF destroys -- but a
# ledger is an artefact committed alongside code, and its writer always emits
# LF. A source tree that disagrees with its own output is a diff waiting to
# happen.
* text=auto eol=lf
